<rml>
<head>
	<title>VaCuus M5 Material Decorators</title>
	<style>
		body
		{
			display: block;
			font-family: LatoLatin;
			font-size: 20px;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			color: #E8E8E8;
		}
		div { display: block; position: absolute; }
		.head { font-size: 24px; color: #FFD24A; }
		.cell
		{
			width: 380px;
			height: 240px;
			background-color: #10141AC0;
			padding: 10px;
			line-height: 30px;
		}
		#translucent { decorator: shader( spike-translucent ); }
		#additive    { decorator: shader( spike-additive ); }
		#opaque      { decorator: shader( spike-opaque ); }
		#mid         { decorator: shader( spike-mid ); }
		#anim        { decorator: shader( spike-anim ); }
	</style>
</head>

<!-- THE MATERIAL-DECORATOR CANVAS (Task 5b, the production tier; the spike's injection
     surface is retired). Each cell's material is a `decorator: shader(spike-*)` key the
     vacuus.M5MatSpike toggle registers through a real UVaCuusStyleSet before this
     document loads, so the keys resolve on their first compile. Decorators paint the
     cell's box UNDER its text (RmlUi paints decoration before content) — the recorded
     z-order, where the spike injected over everything. The document is deliberately
     STATIC: after the settle, every publish it makes is the forced-republish remedy
     keeping the Time-driven #anim cell moving, and with vacuus.MaterialForcedRepublish
     0 that cell FREEZES between publishes — the spec §2(f) fact, still observable. -->
<body>
	<div style="left: 60px; top: 40px;" class="head">VaCuus M5 // MATERIAL DECORATORS</div>

	<div style="left: 60px; top: 96px;">TRANSLUCENT under text</div>
	<div style="left: 60px; top: 130px;" class="cell" id="translucent">
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
	</div>

	<div style="left: 520px; top: 96px;">ADDITIVE under text</div>
	<div style="left: 520px; top: 130px;" class="cell" id="additive">
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
	</div>

	<div style="left: 980px; top: 96px;">OPAQUE (replaces the cell box)</div>
	<div style="left: 980px; top: 130px;" class="cell" id="opaque">
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
	</div>

	<div style="left: 1440px; top: 96px;">MID base (params are game-side, UE-native)</div>
	<div style="left: 1440px; top: 130px;" class="cell" id="mid">
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
	</div>

	<div style="left: 60px; top: 426px;">TIME-ANIMATED (the freeze subject; the remedy keeps it moving)</div>
	<div style="left: 60px; top: 460px; width: 740px;" class="cell" id="anim">
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
		The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog 0123456789.
	</div>

	<div style="left: 60px; top: 760px; width: 740px;" class="cell" id="control">
		CONTROL CELL - no material is ever drawn here; if this text changes between
		two screenshots, the diff is not the material path.
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
